      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T20:39:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it would solve the circular dependency issue.\nBut I think it won\u0027t be good if we combine too much stuff in a single roller.\nWhen there are a lot of dependencies rolled together, one bad dependency will block others from updating.\nAnd while one dependency is being fixed, another can get broken, and in the end the roll never proceeds.\nSo, I\u0027d like to keep all the existing rollers, other than the depot_tools one.\nI see Chromium-\u003eDawn roller as \"build system\" update.\nANGLE, vulkan-deps and SwiftShader do not need to roll together with build system updates.",
      "parentUuid": "8a2e248e_3624561f",
      "revId": "14f11d7169943e092a3a48660c05c854cb96e191",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
